For k173 (note only; nothing else needed in k173's files): the lazy-load result above.
For k181:
- Inside a pp binary $^X is the literal "perl" and $0 is the binary's absolute path, even when started through PATH. A background re-exec (the reference does process.execPath binPath hook __sync-background) must exec $0 alone when packed, never $^X $0.
- Whether PAR_* env vars inherited by such a child change its start: untested.
- Hook budget: floor about 250 ms warm, plus the engine path about +190 ms (status minus --version).
- loaded-modules.pl already runs every hook event (plain, --harness codex, with CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR), so k181's modules join the packed set without edits. Re-measure hooks after k181.
For k167:
- The Debian 13 host build has glibc floor 2.38 (POSIX.so, MIME/Base64.so, libperl.so.5.40). check-binary-libs.sh keeps the house ceiling of 2.31 and fails on that build, as it should.
- A bullseye build (perl:5.40-bullseye is available locally) would link OpenSSL 1.1, which Debian 12+ and Ubuntu 22.04+ do not ship. An https url source needs libssl there, so bundling it (pp -l) or another build image may be needed. Untested.
Drift (not in scope): perl/cpanfile says perl 5.020, but Text::Nunjucks needs 5.40 (k159). dzil build warns that MetaProvides lists Skilletor::Frontmatter::Float and Skilletor::TOML::Float without .pm files.

